  "description": "USDC's EIP-3009 messages on Ethereum, Base and Arbitrum (spec section 15.9, experimental). TransferWithAuthorization and ReceiveWithAuthorization pay `to` once, by a signature that someone else submits (only the payee, for ReceiveWithAuthorization), and CancelAuthorization cancels one that is unused (EIP-3009; Circle stablecoin-evm, FiatTokenV2.sol). x402's `exact` scheme pays by TransferWithAuthorization by default (coinbase/x402, specs/schemes/exact/scheme_exact_evm.md). Only the messages are described: USDC's ABI names transferWithAuthorization, receiveWithAuthorization, cancelAuthorization and permit twice each, which the resolver refuses (O1). Bound to USDC's domain (`USD Coin`, version `2`) and to its contracts, each read on chain on 2026-10-30 (DOMAIN_SEPARATOR, decimals 6, the three type hashes), so a look-alike token gets none of these words.",
